      "text_raw": "This fully-differential ampli-\nfier uses a CMFB of type\none, i.e. with transistors in\nthe linear region (on the\nright).\nThe differential amplifier\nis just a folded cascode\nOTA. Additional capaci-\ntances C with R are\ncomp comp\nused to boost its high-fre-\nquency performance (above\n20 MHz).\nThe CMFB amplifier\nconsists of MOSTs M20/\nM21 in the linear region and\ncurrent mirrors M23/M17\nand M15/M9,10. This is a wide-band amplifier, but at the cost of additional power consumption.\nThe outputs will end up around reference voltage V , as the transistors M19–21 have sizes\nref\nwhich are matched to their currents.",
      "text": "This fully-differential amplifier uses a CMFB of type one, i.e. with transistors in the linear region (on the right). The differential amplifier is just a folded cascode OTA. Additional capacitances C with R are comp comp used to boost its high-frequency performance (above 20 MHz). The CMFB amplifier consists of MOSTs M20/ M21 in the linear region and current mirrors M23/M17 and M15/M9,10. This is a wide-band amplifier, but at the cost of additional power consumption. The outputs will end up around reference voltage V , as the transistors M19–21 have sizes ref which are matched to their currents."
